  "aiContextParagraph": "Following the Deepavali festival, air quality across India's capital has deteriorated to the severe category. Despite existing bans on firecrackers, widespread usage during the holiday has resulted in a thick toxic haze blanketing New Delhi, with pollution levels reported to be over 50 times the limits established by the World Health Organization in certain areas. The smog has also extended to other urban centers, including Mumbai, Chennai, and Hyderabad, where hazardous particulate matter concentrations were recorded. Amid the environmental crisis, political tension has surfaced between the Aam Aadmi Party and the government. Opposition leaders have alleged that official air quality data is being manipulated, claiming that water is being sprayed on monitoring sensors to falsely lower recorded pollution levels, a practice they characterized as both corrupt and dangerous to public health.",
